course: dictionary
lesson: 7540
title: Exact and careful words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Precisely» is a word for being exact. If a train leaves at precisely nine o'clock, it leaves at nine, not at five past or a quarter to. Precisely means exactly, with no mistakes or difference.
explain: The word can also mean carefully and accurately. «Measure the plant precisely» tells you to measure it with care, so your answer is correct. Scientists and builders use the word a lot because they need exact sizes and answers.
explain: People also say «Precisely!» to agree strongly, as in «Yes, precisely!» It means «Yes, exactly that!» Look at the words around it to be sure which meaning the writer means.
fact: Precisely is an adverb, and it comes from the adjective precise.
fact: «Precisely» can mean exactly, with no difference: «at precisely nine o'clock».
fact: «Precisely» can mean carefully and accurately: «measure precisely».
fact: «To be precise» and «more precisely» are phrases that give an exact detail, as in «to be precise, 12.5 cm».
fact: In a story, precisely often tells us an exact time, and in science it tells us an exact measurement.
exercise: «The train leaves at precisely nine o'clock.» What does precisely mean here? | Roughly, around that time | Sometimes | Very quietly | *Exactly, with no difference
exercise: «She measured the plant precisely.» Which word tells you how she measured? | happily | *carefully | slowly | loudly
exercise: Tom asks, «Is that the right answer?» His friend says, «Precisely!» What does she mean? | No, that is wrong | Please be quiet | She is hungry | *Yes, exactly that!
test: «A good steel mould must be shaped extremely precisely.» Why must it be shaped precisely? | *So every part comes out exactly the same | So it looks pretty and bright | So it can float on water | So it is cheap to buy
test: «To be precise, the bridge is 212 metres long.» What does «to be precise» tell you? | The bridge is very short | The bridge is a rough guess | The bridge is a secret | *It gives the exact length
exam: Which word could replace precisely in «She stopped at precisely noon»? | Quietly | Roughly | *Exactly | Happily
